<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!--
  EFT X6100 hexacopter — AAVC 2026 airframe (replaces the x500 quad, 2026-07-22).

  Frame only: links, joints, sensors, landing gear. The flyable model
  (sitl/models/eft_x6100) merge-includes this and adds the 6 motor plugins plus
  the nadir camera.

  Geometry mirrors the REAL bird's PX4 control-allocation table (read off the
  6X on 2026-07-22, airframe 6001 Generic Hexarotor X) scaled to the X6100's
  arm radius, so SITL allocation matches the aircraft:

      CA rotor (FRD)      KM      this model (ENU)   spin
      R0 ( 0.000, +0.500) -0.05   ( 0.000, -0.500)   cw
      R1 ( 0.000, -0.500) +0.05   ( 0.000, +0.500)   ccw
      R2 (+0.433, -0.250) -0.05   (+0.433, +0.250)   cw
      R3 (-0.433, +0.250) +0.05   (-0.433, -0.250)   ccw
      R4 (+0.433, +0.250) +0.05   (+0.433, -0.250)   ccw
      R5 (-0.433, -0.250) -0.05   (-0.433, +0.250)   cw

  PX4 CA is body-FRD (+Y right), SDF is body-ENU (+Y left) => Y is negated.
  KM +0.05 <-> ccw, KM -0.05 <-> cw (verified against the x500, whose rotor_0 is
  front-right / KM +0.05 / ccw). rotor_N here IS PX4 Motor N+1 via
  SIM_GZ_EC_FUNC(N+1) = 101+N in the 22000_gz_eft_x6100 airframe.

  Geometry and masses come from the team's own power-system document
  (Power-System-Guide-1.pdf, 2026-07-22) — NOT guesses:
    frame X6100 wheelbase 1.000 m => arm radius 0.500 m, frame 2.75 kg, MTOW 12 kg
    EFT E5 per arm: 5008/335KV motor + 40 A ESC + 18x6.5" folding prop = 362 g
    planned AUW 8.22 kg  (frame 2.75 + E5 x6 2.17 + 6S 7500 mAh x2 2.10
                          + FC/GPS/power-module 0.50 + companion+camera 0.35
                          + release mech 0.20 + egg 0.15)
    base_link 7.881 kg + 6 x 0.048 kg props + camera 0.05 + lidar 0.001 = 8.22 kg
    Ixx=Iyy 0.34, Izz 0.64 kg.m^2 (362 g per arm at R=0.5 + central box)

  2026-07-25 — SECOND BATTERY: the aircraft now carries TWO of the same DXF 6S
  7500 mAh packs wired in PARALLEL (15,000 mAh at 6S, one pack's voltage), so
  AUW went 7.17 -> 8.22 kg and base_link 6.831 -> 7.881 kg. Hover per motor is
  now 8.22*9.807/6 = 13.44 N => w = sqrt(13.44/3.765e-5) = 597 rad/s =>
  throttle (597-150)/850 = 0.53, which is what MPC_THR_HOVER is set to in
  sitl/px4_patches/22000_gz_eft_x6100 (was 0.48). T/W drops 3.21 -> 2.80
  (23 kg of thrust against 8.22 kg), still ample.
  The inertia tensor is deliberately UNCHANGED: the second pack rides beside
  the first, within ~0.08 m of the CG, so it adds ~1.05*0.08^2 = 0.007 kg.m^2
  (2 % of Ixx) — inside this model's own fidelity, and far below the arm/motor
  terms that set the tensor. Revisit only if the pack ends up mounted well off
  the CG. Energy side of the same change: sitl/aavc_config.yaml `battery`.
  Still to confirm at G5: the real weigh-in, and the landing-gear height/footprint
  (0.30 m assumed here) — that footprint has to fit a 1 m pad.

  Landing gear is 0.30 m tall (skid bottoms at z=-0.298 from base_link) —
  taller than the x500's, which is why the model spawns at z=0.35 and why the
  nadir camera mount was re-derived in eft_x6100/model.sdf.
-->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <model name="eft_x6100_base">
    <!-- Ignored on the live spawn path: PX4 spawns this model through a merged
         <include> — and (CORRECTED 2026-08-14, sibling-session finding,
         verified with `gz sdf -p`) that merge DOES carry this pose: gz
         creates a _merged__eft_x6100_base__model__ frame at +0.35 in the
         eft_x6100 model frame and every link here rides on it. Any TOP-
         LEVEL addition in eft_x6100/model.sdf must therefore author its z
         in the MODEL frame = base-frame z + 0.35 (the old comment claimed
         the pose was ignored, which is how the camera/cargo ended up 0.35
         too low). PX4_GZ_MODEL_POSE in launch_sitl.sh positions the MODEL
         origin at spawn on top of this. -->
    <pose>0 0 0.35 0 0 0</pose>
    <self_collide>false</self_collide>
    <static>false</static>
    <!-- WIND (added 2026-08-15). gz's WindEffects plugin only pushes links that
         OPT IN with enable_wind — it is off by default. Both worlds have carried
         the plugin (and aavc_config.yaml a wind_sitl block) since the field was
         built, so everything LOOKED like wind was modelled, but no link ever
         asked for it: every validated flight to date, G4/G4' included, flew in
         perfectly still air. KMITL is exposed and windy, which makes still-air
         results the wrong thing to trust. Set here on the airframe root so it
         reaches base_link; the cargo boxes stay out of it (a 90 g box on a
         breaking joint gains nothing from wind drag but can jitter the solver). -->
    <enable_wind>true</enable_wind>
    <link name="base_link">
      <inertial>
        <mass>7.881</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.34</ixx>
          <ixy>0</ixy>
          <ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.34</iyy>
          <iyz>0</iyz>
          <izz>0.64</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <gravity>true</gravity>
      <velocity_decay/>

      <!-- centre body -->
      <visual name="body_visual">
        <pose>0 0 0.02 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.18</radius>
            <length>0.09</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.15 0.15 0.15 1</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <!-- nose marker so heading is readable in the GUI -->
      <visual name="nose_visual">
        <pose>0.20 0 0.02 0 1.5708 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.02</radius>
            <length>0.10</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.8 0.1 0.1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.9 0.15 0.15 1</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!-- 6 arms at +/-30, +/-90, +/-150 deg (hexa-X: no arm on the nose) -->
      <visual name="arm_0">
        <pose>0 -0.325 0.03 0 1.5708 -1.5708</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.0125</radius><length>0.35</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="arm_1">
        <pose>0 0.325 0.03 0 1.5708 1.5708</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.0125</radius><length>0.35</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="arm_2">
        <pose>0.2815 0.1625 0.03 0 1.5708 0.5236</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.0125</radius><length>0.35</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="arm_3">
        <pose>-0.2815 -0.1625 0.03 0 1.5708 -2.6180</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.0125</radius><length>0.35</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="arm_4">
        <pose>0.2815 -0.1625 0.03 0 1.5708 -0.5236</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.0125</radius><length>0.35</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="arm_5">
        <pose>-0.2815 0.1625 0.03 0 1.5708 2.6180</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder><radius>0.0125</radius><length>0.35</length></cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>

      <!-- motor cans, one per rotor station -->
      <visual name="motor_can_0">
        <pose>0 -0.50 0.055 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.028</radius><length>0.05</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_can_1">
        <pose>0 0.50 0.055 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.028</radius><length>0.05</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_can_2">
        <pose>0.433 0.25 0.055 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.028</radius><length>0.05</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_can_3">
        <pose>-0.433 -0.25 0.055 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.028</radius><length>0.05</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_can_4">
        <pose>0.433 -0.25 0.055 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.028</radius><length>0.05</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="motor_can_5">
        <pose>-0.433 0.25 0.055 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.028</radius><length>0.05</length></cylinder></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.3 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>

      <!-- landing gear: 4 legs + 2 skid rails, 0.30 m tall -->
      <visual name="gear_leg_0">
        <pose>0.20 0.32 -0.15 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.025 0.26</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gear_leg_1">
        <pose>0.20 -0.32 -0.15 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.025 0.26</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gear_leg_2">
        <pose>-0.20 0.32 -0.15 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.025 0.26</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gear_leg_3">
        <pose>-0.20 -0.32 -0.15 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.025 0.025 0.26</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gear_rail_left">
        <pose>0 0.32 -0.283 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.60 0.03 0.03</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="gear_rail_right">
        <pose>0 -0.32 -0.283 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.60 0.03 0.03</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</ambient><diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>

      <!-- Payload-release servo rack (KMUTNB spec 2026-08-11): 4 latch servos
           in a rectangle at (±0.10, ±0.035, 0) — ON the CG plane exactly
           (user spec; z moved -0.04 -> 0 on 2026-08-12). The release is
           DO_SET_ACTUATOR -> SIM_GZ_SV_FUNC1..4 -> payload_detach_bridge. -->
      <visual name="drop_servo_0">
        <pose>0.10 0.035 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.030 0.015 0.030</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.15 0.15 0.60 1</ambient><diffuse>0.2 0.2 0.8 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="drop_servo_1">
        <pose>-0.10 -0.035 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.030 0.015 0.030</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.15 0.15 0.60 1</ambient><diffuse>0.2 0.2 0.8 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="drop_servo_2">
        <pose>0.10 -0.035 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.030 0.015 0.030</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.15 0.15 0.60 1</ambient><diffuse>0.2 0.2 0.8 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="drop_servo_3">
        <pose>-0.10 0.035 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.030 0.015 0.030</size></box></geometry>
        <material><ambient>0.15 0.15 0.60 1</ambient><diffuse>0.2 0.2 0.8 1</diffuse></material>
      </visual>

      <!-- collisions: centre body + the two skid rails that actually touch down.
           Contact params copied from the x500 (min_depth/max_vel keep the
           touchdown from bouncing). -->
      <collision name="base_link_collision_body">
        <pose>0 0 0.02 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.36 0.36 0.08</size></box></geometry>
        <surface>
          <!-- bitmask 0xfd = everything EXCEPT the cargo boxes (0x02): the
               boxes' tops sit AT the CG plane inside this volume (user
               z-spec 2026-08-12) — see cargo_payload/model.sdf. -->
          <contact><collide_bitmask>0xfd</collide_bitmask>
            <ode><min_depth>0.001</min_depth><max_vel>0</max_vel></ode></contact>
          <friction><ode/></friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>
      <collision name="base_link_collision_rail_left">
        <pose>0 0.32 -0.283 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.60 0.03 0.03</size></box></geometry>
        <surface>
          <!-- 0xfd like the body (sibling-session report 2026-08-14): the
               rails carried the DEFAULT 0xffff, so a shed 18 cm box standing
               between the skids could catch a rail during climb-out and
               lever the aircraft (visible lurch at pad drops). The real rack
               is built not to snag; rails<->ground/pad still collide. -->
          <contact><collide_bitmask>0xfd</collide_bitmask>
            <ode><min_depth>0.001</min_depth><max_vel>0</max_vel></ode></contact>
          <friction><ode/></friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>
      <collision name="base_link_collision_rail_right">
        <pose>0 -0.32 -0.283 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.60 0.03 0.03</size></box></geometry>
        <surface>
          <contact><collide_bitmask>0xfd</collide_bitmask>
            <ode><min_depth>0.001</min_depth><max_vel>0</max_vel></ode></contact>
          <friction><ode/></friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>

      <sensor name="air_pressure_sensor" type="air_pressure">
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>50</update_rate>
        <air_pressure>
          <pressure>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <mean>0</mean>
              <stddev>0.01</stddev>
            </noise>
          </pressure>
        </air_pressure>
      </sensor>
      <sensor name="imu_sensor" type="imu">
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>250</update_rate>
        <imu>
          <angular_velocity>
            <x>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.00018665</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>3.8785e-05</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>1000</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </x>
            <y>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.00018665</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>3.8785e-05</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>1000</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </y>
            <z>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.00018665</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>3.8785e-05</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>1000</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </z>
          </angular_velocity>
          <linear_acceleration>
            <x>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.00186</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>0.006</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>300</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </x>
            <y>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.00186</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>0.006</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>300</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </y>
            <z>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.00186</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>0.006</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>300</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </z>
          </linear_acceleration>
        </imu>
      </sensor>
      <!-- PX4 v1.17's GZBridge subscribes the model magnetometer unconditionally
           for multicopters; without it EKF2 never gets a heading and arming is
           denied (silent — the subscribe just never delivers). Block copied from
           upstream v1.17 x500_base. -->
      <sensor name="magnetometer_sensor" type="magnetometer">
        <gz_frame_id>base_link</gz_frame_id>
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>100</update_rate>
        <magnetometer>
          <x>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <stddev>0.0001</stddev>
            </noise>
          </x>
          <y>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <stddev>0.0001</stddev>
            </noise>
          </y>
          <z>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <stddev>0.0001</stddev>
            </noise>
          </z>
        </magnetometer>
      </sensor>
      <sensor name="navsat_sensor" type="navsat">
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>30</update_rate>
      </sensor>
    </link>

    <!-- Downward rangefinder = the real bird's Benewake TFmini-S (0.1-12 m).
         Link/sensor names are the PX4 GZBridge contract (lidar_sensor_link /
         "lidar"); the rotation is upstream x500_lidar_down's so the bridge
         auto-detects ROTATION_DOWNWARD_FACING. SIM_GZ_EN_LIDAR defaults to 1.
         KMUTNB spec 2026-08-11: mounted 0.25 m below the CG, same plane as the
         nadir camera (matching the real aircraft). Landed the emitter sits at
         ~0.048 m AGL — under its own 0.1 m minimum range, so the reading is
         invalid while parked; harmless (EKF2 simply drops rng aiding until
         airborne, exactly as the real TFmini-S behaves on the skids). -->
    <joint name="lidar_sensor_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent>base_link</parent>
      <child>lidar_sensor_link</child>
    </joint>
    <link name="lidar_sensor_link">
      <pose relative_to="base_link">0 0 -0.25 0 1.57 0</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.001</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.00001</ixx>
          <iyy>0.00001</iyy>
          <izz>0.00001</izz>
          <ixy>0.0</ixy>
          <ixz>0.0</ixz>
          <iyz>0.0</iyz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <sensor name='lidar' type='gpu_lidar'>
        <gz_frame_id>lidar_sensor_link</gz_frame_id>
        <pose>0 0 0 3.14 0 0</pose>
        <!-- Every update is an offscreen render pass, on the dGPU this host has
             already hard-frozen under SITL render load. Its only consumer is
             EKF2 height aiding through the gz bridge, which is fully served at
             10 Hz for a 0.1-12 m band, so the extra 20 renders a second bought
             nothing. (Upstream x500_lidar_down ships 50.) -->
        <update_rate>10</update_rate>
        <ray>
          <scan>
            <horizontal>
              <samples>1</samples>
              <resolution>1</resolution>
              <min_angle>0</min_angle>
              <max_angle>0</max_angle>
            </horizontal>
            <vertical>
              <samples>1</samples>
              <resolution>1</resolution>
              <min_angle>0</min_angle>
              <max_angle>0</max_angle>
            </vertical>
          </scan>
          <range>
            <min>0.1</min>
            <max>12.0</max>
            <resolution>0.01</resolution>
          </range>
        </ray>
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <!-- Ray markers are a GUI-only nicety and the stack runs headless. -->
        <visualize>false</visualize>
      </sensor>
    </link>

    <!-- rotors: link N == PX4 Motor N+1 (see header table) -->
    <link name="rotor_0">
      <gravity>true</gravity>
      <self_collide>false</self_collide>
      <velocity_decay/>
      <pose>0 -0.50 0.09 0 0 0</pose>
      <inertial>
        <mass>0.048</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>2.0e-06</ixx>
          <iyy>8.30e-04</iyy>
          <!-- thin-plate: izz = ixx + iyy. gz rejects the whole model if
               izz > ixx + iyy (triangle inequality), so keep it at/below. -->
          <izz>8.30e-04</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <visual name="rotor_0_visual">
        <pose>-0.036 -0.240 -0.018 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1.385 1.385 1.385</scale>
            <uri>model://x500_base/meshes/1345_prop_cw.stl</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.15 0.15 0.15 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <collision name="rotor_0_collision">
        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><box><size>0.457 0.028 0.0012</size></box></geometry>
        <surface>
          <contact><ode><min_depth>0.001</min_depth><max_vel>0</max_vel></ode></contact>
          <friction><ode/></friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>
    </link>
    <joint name="rotor_0_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent>base_link</parent>
      <child>rotor_0</child>
